 ## Deferred interfaces
 
 PGN import (`import-pgn`) produces normalized `GameRecord`s with explicit
-provenance; a FEN setup tag yields `history_complete: false`. Bulk PGN ingestion
+provenance; a FEN setup tag yields `history_complete: false`. `opening-tree` imports every game of
+one PGN file with the same rules and counts main-line move sequences to a
+bounded depth (at most 12 plies), optionally leaving out moves played in fewer
+than `--min-count` games. Nodes are move sequences, not positions, so
+transpositions stay separate; games from a setup position are counted as
+skipped rather than merged into the tree. Siblings are ordered by count, then
+by first appearance in the file. One game that fails to import refuses the
+whole file. Bulk PGN ingestion
 must stream and cap resources. Bulk eval ingestion
 must stream, cap resources, preserve depth/node metadata and retain cp-versus-mate
 semantics. The current in-memory JSONL reader is for bounded fixtures only.
